1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,151
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:07,151 --> 00:00:10,917
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,917 --> 00:00:13,306
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:13,306 --> 00:00:14,316
Give me your hand.

5
00:00:14,316 --> 00:00:15,944
What for?

6
00:00:16,157 --> 00:00:17,765
My puppy.

7
00:00:18,261 --> 00:00:19,868
Hey, we ordered something delicious for you.

8
00:00:19,868 --> 00:00:21,358
Aren’t you guys spoiling me too much?

9
00:00:21,358 --> 00:00:22,718
We were scared out of our minds.

10
00:00:22,718 --> 00:00:24,647
Thank you, guys, for worrying about me.

11
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:25,857
You’re welcome.

12
00:00:25,857 --> 00:00:27,321
I’ll take P’Niran home.

13
00:00:27,321 --> 00:00:28,922
We’re going the same way anyway.

14
00:00:28,922 --> 00:00:30,139
I have a question.

15
00:00:30,375 --> 00:00:31,877
Can we be a couple now?

16
00:00:32,042 --> 00:00:33,070
Turn your face toward me.

17
00:00:33,235 --> 00:00:34,796
I’m not going to answer directly.

18
00:01:50,075 --> 00:01:52,255
I thought you left the lights on.

19
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:53,713
I was coming in to turn them off.

20
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:56,957
It’s past your bedtime.

21
00:01:57,690 --> 00:01:58,783
Why haven’t you gone to bed?

22
00:02:01,336 --> 00:02:02,624
I couldn’t sleep,

23
00:02:02,742 --> 00:02:04,800
so I got up to read some more.

24
00:02:11,583 --> 00:02:12,730
What’s on your mind?

25
00:02:13,155 --> 00:02:14,300
Why couldn’t you sleep?

26
00:02:16,616 --> 00:02:17,696
P’Cheewin.

27
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:18,991
Hmm?

28
00:02:19,795 --> 00:02:22,009
How does it feel to be in love?

29
00:02:26,287 --> 00:02:30,000
I like him, but I just don’t know what’s next.

30
00:02:31,536 --> 00:02:34,358
Am I trying to win him over
the way people do?

31
00:02:36,131 --> 00:02:38,196
Should I do anything more?

32
00:02:38,811 --> 00:02:40,288
It’s so hard.

33
00:02:41,162 --> 00:02:43,527
Even harder than
learning about the universe.

34
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:45,809
I’m so confused.

35
00:02:48,929 --> 00:02:53,920
Every time I see him, I’m always
thinking about what we should talk about.

36
00:02:56,922 --> 00:03:03,243
I keep accidentally talking about
what I’m interested in and what I know.

37
00:03:04,590 --> 00:03:06,969
What has he said?

38
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:12,172
He always seems to listen
until I finish talking.

39
00:03:12,810 --> 00:03:14,983
Oh, then that’s good.

40
00:03:15,361 --> 00:03:16,651
How is that not good?

41
00:03:17,431 --> 00:03:18,395
It’s good.

42
00:03:19,033 --> 00:03:21,370
I want to keep seeing him every day.

43
00:03:22,174 --> 00:03:24,155
I want to stay by his side like this forever.

44
00:03:24,864 --> 00:03:26,554
Actually, it’s like—

45
00:03:26,554 --> 00:03:28,197
It’s like Dad and Mom, right?

46
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:36,351
When Dad goes to work,
Mom follows to cheer him on.

47
00:03:37,131 --> 00:03:38,739
They’re always together.

48
00:03:39,779 --> 00:03:41,022
That’s what you mean, right?

49
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,083
Yes.

50
00:03:45,446 --> 00:03:46,532
Well, then.

51
00:03:47,572 --> 00:03:49,174
Just ask Niran to be your boyfriend.

52
00:03:52,223 --> 00:03:53,620
I’ve already asked.

53
00:03:53,762 --> 00:03:54,442
What?

54
00:03:56,026 --> 00:03:57,135
Already?

55
00:03:59,333 --> 00:04:00,654
What did he say?

56
00:04:01,127 --> 00:04:02,870
Did he reject you?

57
00:04:03,934 --> 00:04:05,764
He didn’t say anything.

58
00:04:10,089 --> 00:04:11,307
Hmm…

59
00:04:13,647 --> 00:04:15,041
Then ask again.

60
00:04:15,703 --> 00:04:17,608
Ask him again when you see him.

61
00:04:18,364 --> 00:04:19,801
Ask until he gives you an answer.

62
00:04:20,605 --> 00:04:21,914
One more thing.

63
00:04:22,765 --> 00:04:24,339
Make a bigger move.

64
00:04:25,095 --> 00:04:26,612
A billion times bigger.

65
00:04:29,377 --> 00:04:31,143
It’s actually a good idea to keep asking.

66
00:04:31,805 --> 00:04:33,294
I’m not going to answer directly.

67
00:04:49,959 --> 00:04:51,908
Love isn’t complicated.

68
00:04:52,570 --> 00:04:56,250
Whatever you feel,
just follow your feelings.

69
00:04:58,897 --> 00:05:00,498
I’m rooting for you, brother.

70
00:05:05,390 --> 00:05:07,838
P’Niran will accept my love one day.

71
00:05:08,145 --> 00:05:10,911
No matter how many
million light-years away it is,

72
00:05:11,266 --> 00:05:13,153
I will get there.

73
00:05:15,044 --> 00:05:15,736
Mm.

74
00:05:39,574 --> 00:05:42,515
Are you sure
you don’t want to bring your crutch?

75
00:05:44,921 --> 00:05:45,876
I’ll be fine.

76
00:05:47,034 --> 00:05:48,871
You could’ve just waited inside your house.

77
00:05:50,667 --> 00:05:51,892
I only injured one leg.

78
00:05:51,892 --> 00:05:52,941
I can still walk on the other.

79
00:05:52,941 --> 00:05:54,711
Hey, come on.

80
00:05:54,711 --> 00:05:56,717
You’re already bothering him,
and now you’re getting on his nerves too?

81
00:05:58,962 --> 00:06:00,203
Not a bother at all.

82
00:06:00,368 --> 00:06:01,545
I’m free this week.

83
00:06:01,545 --> 00:06:03,786
I’m dropping my brother off at school anyway.

84
00:06:04,755 --> 00:06:06,356
We really are bothering you.

85
00:06:06,876 --> 00:06:08,975
Are you sure
you don’t want us to help pay for gas?

86
00:06:08,975 --> 00:06:10,310
It’s expensive these days.

87
00:06:10,523 --> 00:06:11,529
It’s no trouble at all.

88
00:06:11,529 --> 00:06:12,700
I’m very happy to help.

89
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,152
Besides,

90
00:06:14,530 --> 00:06:17,146
Cheewa gets company on his ride to school.

91
00:06:18,682 --> 00:06:20,163
Alright then.

92
00:06:20,423 --> 00:06:21,408
But still,

93
00:06:21,692 --> 00:06:23,336
please take this with you to eat.

94
00:06:24,187 --> 00:06:24,898
Thank you.

95
00:06:24,898 --> 00:06:25,891
No worries.

96
00:06:27,805 --> 00:06:28,599
Cheewa.

97
00:06:28,883 --> 00:06:29,653
Cheewa.

98
00:06:29,748 --> 00:06:30,427
Yes?

99
00:06:30,427 --> 00:06:31,346
Say thank you to him.

100
00:06:31,346 --> 00:06:32,313
Thank you so much.

101
00:06:32,313 --> 00:06:33,265
No problem.

102
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:37,289
When I’m free, please let me drive Cheewa and Niran to school for a change.

103
00:06:37,951 --> 00:06:39,137
Of course.

104
00:06:39,562 --> 00:06:41,128
I should get going.

105
00:06:41,128 --> 00:06:41,919
Okay.

106
00:06:42,321 --> 00:06:43,598
Bye.

107
00:06:44,672 --> 00:06:45,673
Drive safe.

108
00:06:45,673 --> 00:06:46,382
I will.

109
00:06:48,202 --> 00:06:49,102
Cheewa.

110
00:06:49,102 --> 00:06:49,765
Here.

111
00:06:59,288 --> 00:07:00,393
Why are they staring?

112
00:07:06,751 --> 00:07:08,765
Why does our school
have morning assemblies?

113
00:07:08,978 --> 00:07:09,824
I know, right?

114
00:07:15,874 --> 00:07:16,753
Whoa.

115
00:07:17,746 --> 00:07:18,836
Do you want to take some days off?

116
00:07:18,954 --> 00:07:20,872
You don’t want me to graduate
at the same time as you guys?

117
00:07:20,872 --> 00:07:22,277
It’s just a hurt leg.

118
00:07:22,632 --> 00:07:23,758
I could still kick you right now,

119
00:07:24,372 --> 00:07:25,523
Come on.

120
00:07:25,688 --> 00:07:27,017
You’re so tough, huh?

121
00:07:27,679 --> 00:07:30,753
Next time,
don’t push yourself too hard again. Got it?

122
00:07:31,131 --> 00:07:32,969
We’re all worried about you.

123
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,061
But…

124
00:07:37,339 --> 00:07:39,517
probably not as much as Cheewa is.

125
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:47,698
Why the hell are you shy?

126
00:07:48,502 --> 00:07:50,749
You weren’t shy when you
rode on his back home the other day.

127
00:07:51,954 --> 00:07:53,514
Well, my leg hurt.

128
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:55,420
And he lives near my house.

129
00:07:55,420 --> 00:07:56,539
I’m shy? My ass.

130
00:07:56,776 --> 00:07:58,407
Or do you want to give me a piggyback ride?

131
00:07:58,856 --> 00:07:59,356
Huh?

132
00:07:59,356 --> 00:08:00,515
All three of you.

133
00:08:00,515 --> 00:08:01,176
There it is.

134
00:08:01,318 --> 00:08:02,393
You’re shy right now.

135
00:08:03,622 --> 00:08:05,052
What do you mean? I’m not shy.

136
00:08:05,548 --> 00:08:06,657
You’re shy.

137
00:08:06,799 --> 00:08:07,844
Admit it.

138
00:08:08,175 --> 00:08:09,321
Will you guys stop teasing me already?

139
00:08:12,157 --> 00:08:14,260
Yes, please stop teasing him.

140
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:14,911
Mm.

141
00:08:15,336 --> 00:08:17,262
P’Niran doesn’t want you guys to know
he’s shy.

142
00:08:20,973 --> 00:08:22,783
Are you on my side or theirs?

143
00:08:22,925 --> 00:08:24,570
Huh? Whose side are you really on?

144
00:08:25,846 --> 00:08:27,058
I could be by your side.

145
00:08:27,058 --> 00:08:27,803
Yeah.

146
00:08:27,803 --> 00:08:29,181
If you’re still not taken.

147
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:36,178
Guys.

148
00:08:36,674 --> 00:08:37,562
Yes?

149
00:08:38,696 --> 00:08:40,355
Can I date your friend now?

150
00:08:41,064 --> 00:08:42,657
Huh?

151
00:08:44,075 --> 00:08:46,977
I asked him, but he wouldn’t answer.

152
00:08:47,166 --> 00:08:48,685
So I’m asking you guys.

153
00:08:48,685 --> 00:08:49,718
You’re his best friends.

154
00:08:49,718 --> 00:08:50,923
I thought you might know the answer.

155
00:08:51,679 --> 00:08:53,372
I might be good at studying,

156
00:08:53,727 --> 00:08:55,564
but I know nothing about this.

157
00:08:57,266 --> 00:08:58,136
Seriously.

158
00:08:59,767 --> 00:09:01,410
Let’s change the topic already.

159
00:09:01,410 --> 00:09:03,219
If not, I’ll throw you one by one.

160
00:09:03,219 --> 00:09:04,838
And we’re going to
get food from Auntie Tang’s today.

161
00:09:05,122 --> 00:09:06,336
Not anywhere else.

162
00:09:06,336 --> 00:09:07,291
What’s wrong with you?

163
00:09:07,291 --> 00:09:08,310
It’s still early.

164
00:09:08,310 --> 00:09:09,599
We haven’t even started lining up yet.

165
00:09:10,072 --> 00:09:11,054
You’re getting nervous already.

166
00:09:11,361 --> 00:09:12,000
Yeah.

167
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,025
What’s wrong?

168
00:09:14,584 --> 00:09:16,355
Auntie Tang’s as always. Never changes.

169
00:09:17,608 --> 00:09:18,978
Loyal to one and only.

170
00:09:20,963 --> 00:09:24,037
I think Cheewa is getting down bad.

171
00:09:24,037 --> 00:09:25,150
What have you done to my brother?

172
00:09:25,150 --> 00:09:25,737
Yeah.

173
00:09:25,737 --> 00:09:26,783
Why did you change him?

174
00:09:26,783 --> 00:09:27,941
Let’s go get some dessert.

175
00:09:30,564 --> 00:09:31,605
Stay here.

176
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:34,915
I’m going to buy a lollipop
to sweeten things up for you.

177
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:37,371
Okay.

178
00:09:37,371 --> 00:09:38,387
Get me the same flavor.

179
00:09:42,181 --> 00:09:43,556
Did you know?

180
00:09:45,399 --> 00:09:47,072
I like you just the same.

181
00:09:47,686 --> 00:09:49,680
Gosh.

182
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:50,597
He’s down bad.

183
00:09:54,407 --> 00:09:55,873
No one has a crush on me.

184
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:58,169
I want some dessert too.

185
00:10:02,233 --> 00:10:03,227
“Wait here.”

186
00:10:03,865 --> 00:10:05,619
“I’m going to get you some dessert.”

187
00:10:07,010 --> 00:10:08,787
By the way, Niran,

188
00:10:09,590 --> 00:10:11,147
can I ask you something?

189
00:10:15,472 --> 00:10:17,250
So, what’s the deal?

190
00:10:17,463 --> 00:10:19,066
He’s coming on to you this hard.

191
00:10:19,066 --> 00:10:20,524
Has he asked you to be his boyfriend?

192
00:10:21,233 --> 00:10:22,459
When will you become a couple?

193
00:10:22,459 --> 00:10:23,404
Or are you already a couple?

194
00:10:25,627 --> 00:10:27,035
We’re not dating!

195
00:10:27,035 --> 00:10:28,093
Sit down properly.

196
00:10:31,662 --> 00:10:33,863
You guys look freaking hilarious.

197
00:10:36,959 --> 00:10:37,869
My friends.

198
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:42,801
Damn it.

199
00:10:46,393 --> 00:10:47,208
Well…

200
00:10:49,311 --> 00:10:50,631
Yeah, you got it.

201
00:10:50,631 --> 00:10:53,935
The kid seems to keep trying to win me over.

202
00:10:54,455 --> 00:10:55,416
You guys know that.

203
00:10:55,416 --> 00:10:56,432
I’m just going along with it.

204
00:10:56,999 --> 00:10:58,183
We don’t know.

205
00:10:59,266 --> 00:11:00,397
Yeah, what do you mean
by going along with it?

206
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:06,599
Do you like him hitting on you?

207
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:14,286
You guys give me such a headache,
you know?

208
00:11:23,041 --> 00:11:24,737
What’s with you guys?

209
00:11:26,651 --> 00:11:28,220
Whoa!

210
00:11:28,362 --> 00:11:29,320
You’re pretty heavy.

211
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:31,201
Dude, go on a diet. I’m begging you.

212
00:11:31,201 --> 00:11:32,542
You’re really heavy.

213
00:11:32,542 --> 00:11:33,743
So damn heavy.

214
00:11:33,743 --> 00:11:34,586
I can walk.

215
00:11:34,586 --> 00:11:35,471
Ouch!

216
00:11:36,582 --> 00:11:37,274
Sorry.

217
00:11:38,638 --> 00:11:39,767
You guys are the worst.

218
00:11:40,972 --> 00:11:42,832
We’ll go.

219
00:11:42,832 --> 00:11:44,582
You two can help each other walk.

220
00:11:45,078 --> 00:11:46,227
I don’t want to wait.

221
00:11:46,227 --> 00:11:48,866
Romantic scenes are always in slow motion.

222
00:11:48,866 --> 00:11:50,209
We can’t wait that long.

223
00:11:51,225 --> 00:11:52,240
See you later.

224
00:11:57,558 --> 00:11:58,574
You’re so extra.

225
00:11:58,574 --> 00:11:59,542
It’s just lunch.

226
00:11:59,542 --> 00:12:00,721
I could’ve gone with my friends.

227
00:12:00,981 --> 00:12:04,353
But I want to go with you
and I have something to tell you.

228
00:12:05,535 --> 00:12:07,822
P’Cheewin is picking us up
a bit late this evening.

229
00:12:07,822 --> 00:12:10,290
I need to prepare for the tri-school game.

230
00:12:10,290 --> 00:12:12,101
Oh, it’s coming up?

231
00:12:12,101 --> 00:12:14,225
Yes, it’s next week.

232
00:12:14,532 --> 00:12:17,121
That’s why the whole student council is busy.

233
00:12:17,121 --> 00:12:19,044
It’s okay. Just do your work. I can wait.

234
00:12:19,044 --> 00:12:20,680
Do you want to stay with me while I work?

235
00:12:21,790 --> 00:12:23,199
But…

236
00:12:24,617 --> 00:12:26,014
I don’t think you should.

237
00:12:26,888 --> 00:12:28,919
There are so many people
on the basketball court.

238
00:12:28,919 --> 00:12:30,668
You’re not feeling very well.

239
00:12:31,425 --> 00:12:32,675
Just do whatever you want.

240
00:12:32,675 --> 00:12:34,499
Right now, I’m hungry.

241
00:12:34,499 --> 00:12:36,079
I’m starving.
Let’s go get something to eat.

242
00:12:37,095 --> 00:12:38,038
You’re right.

243
00:12:38,038 --> 00:12:39,983
I’m really craving food from Auntie Tang.

244
00:12:39,983 --> 00:12:41,112
Let me help you walk.

245
00:12:42,814 --> 00:12:44,437
Thank god you’re not carrying me
like last time.

246
00:12:47,391 --> 00:12:48,691
Walk carefully.

247
00:12:49,211 --> 00:12:50,350
Carry me then.

248
00:12:52,241 --> 00:12:53,746
Do you have a lot of work at school?

249
00:12:54,384 --> 00:12:57,894
Cheewa told me to pick you guys up late
because he needs to prepare some stuff.

250
00:12:59,194 --> 00:13:00,283
Yes.

251
00:13:00,283 --> 00:13:02,591
We have a school event next week.

252
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:03,233
Oh.

253
00:13:03,233 --> 00:13:07,261
It’s a sports event where students from
three schools come together to compete.

254
00:13:08,537 --> 00:13:11,983
Our school is the host this year.

255
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:12,711
I see.

256
00:13:13,869 --> 00:13:15,876
So the student council
needs to prepare for that.

257
00:13:18,689 --> 00:13:20,546
Are you competing in anything?

258
00:13:21,964 --> 00:13:22,651
Oh.

259
00:13:23,124 --> 00:13:25,125
Look at my leg.
I don’t think I can compete with anyone.

260
00:13:25,125 --> 00:13:26,066
Oh, right.

261
00:13:26,987 --> 00:13:29,116
Other people have been practicing sports.

262
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:30,236
Meanwhile,

263
00:13:30,543 --> 00:13:33,778
I’ve been taking naps while waiting
for Cheewa in the student council’s room.

264
00:13:34,605 --> 00:13:35,496
That’s good.

265
00:13:35,898 --> 00:13:38,324
Wait until you recover
before you get back into action again.

266
00:13:39,152 --> 00:13:39,827
Yeah.

267
00:13:44,010 --> 00:13:45,357
By the way, Niran,

268
00:13:46,751 --> 00:13:48,464
are you happy with Cheewa?

269
00:13:52,056 --> 00:13:53,109
Yeah, I am.

270
00:13:53,882 --> 00:13:56,358
Then I’ll be picking you up
and dropping you off at school

271
00:13:56,665 --> 00:13:57,858
until your leg has healed.

272
00:13:57,858 --> 00:13:59,771
Oh, you really don’t have to.

273
00:13:59,771 --> 00:14:01,897
I don’t want to bother you.

274
00:14:01,897 --> 00:14:03,001
I can ask my dad to pick me up.

275
00:14:03,001 --> 00:14:04,200
Hey.
It’s okay.

276
00:14:05,121 --> 00:14:06,252
I can drop you off.

277
00:14:06,748 --> 00:14:09,165
I have to drop Cheewa off anyway

278
00:14:09,307 --> 00:14:10,708
Besides,

279
00:14:10,921 --> 00:14:13,467
I get food from your dad
every morning.

280
00:14:14,152 --> 00:14:15,384
That’s amazing.

281
00:14:17,818 --> 00:14:21,325
Alright, whatever’s convenient for you.

282
00:14:21,325 --> 00:14:22,548
I’m okay with anything.

283
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:26,499
Thank you, big bro.

284
00:14:30,611 --> 00:14:31,906
Of course, little bro.

285
00:15:06,933 --> 00:15:08,304
(Hi, P’Niran.)

286
00:15:08,304 --> 00:15:08,804
Oh.

287
00:15:08,804 --> 00:15:09,794
- Were you asleep?
- (What’s up?)

288
00:15:09,794 --> 00:15:10,593
Sorry.

289
00:15:11,538 --> 00:15:12,856
I can talk.

290
00:15:13,967 --> 00:15:15,772
Is everything alright?

291
00:15:19,294 --> 00:15:23,639
Oh, I just wanted to ask if we’re meeting
at the same time tomorrow morning.

292
00:15:24,773 --> 00:15:26,268
(Same time.)

293
00:15:27,379 --> 00:15:30,202
Or do you want to leave earlier or later?

294
00:15:30,816 --> 00:15:32,833
No, I’m just asking.

295
00:15:34,393 --> 00:15:35,673
Okay.

296
00:15:36,382 --> 00:15:38,275
Then let’s meet at the same time.

297
00:15:38,582 --> 00:15:39,776
(Were you exhausted today?)

298
00:15:40,296 --> 00:15:41,344
You fell asleep in the car too.

299
00:15:44,771 --> 00:15:46,064
(I’m so exhausted.)

300
00:15:48,286 --> 00:15:50,684
I want to keep talking to you,

301
00:15:53,024 --> 00:15:56,659
but it feels like I’m about to pass out, P’Niran.

302
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:00,312
You can go back to sleep.

303
00:16:00,477 --> 00:16:01,451
We can talk tomorrow.

304
00:16:03,082 --> 00:16:04,226
(P’Niran.)

305
00:16:06,093 --> 00:16:06,855
Yes?

306
00:16:07,824 --> 00:16:10,015
I might’ve been pretty busy

307
00:16:10,889 --> 00:16:12,430
with the school event lately,

308
00:16:13,943 --> 00:16:16,753
(and I might not have time
to tell you this often,)

309
00:16:17,746 --> 00:16:19,765
(but I’m still the same in every way.)

310
00:16:21,372 --> 00:16:23,113
I miss you every day.

311
00:16:24,838 --> 00:16:26,620
(I still like you the same.)

312
00:16:28,157 --> 00:16:28,832
Mm.

313
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:30,374
Go to sleep.

314
00:16:32,572 --> 00:16:33,953
Okay.

315
00:16:35,017 --> 00:16:36,526
Good night.

316
00:16:39,339 --> 00:16:41,737
Mm. Good night.

317
00:16:42,966 --> 00:16:44,296
(Got it.)

318
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:51,493
You can pick me up later tomorrow

319
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,776
so you can have more time to sleep.

320
00:17:00,143 --> 00:17:00,780
Cheewa.

321
00:17:01,962 --> 00:17:02,727
Cheewa.

322
00:17:04,121 --> 00:17:05,031
Are you asleep?

323
00:17:07,631 --> 00:17:10,390
(Okay. I’ll hang up.)

324
00:17:12,257 --> 00:17:13,450
Tomorrow,

325
00:17:15,932 --> 00:17:17,178
I’ll be waiting to see you.

326
00:17:33,910 --> 00:17:36,051
The game starts at 1.
Wanna go watch?

327
00:17:36,523 --> 00:17:37,313
You mean basketball?

328
00:17:37,928 --> 00:17:39,974
Yes, come watch me compete.

329
00:17:54,436 --> 00:17:55,292
Hello.

330
00:17:58,269 --> 00:17:58,935
Hey, guys.

331
00:17:59,443 --> 00:18:00,478
I saw Jace,

332
00:18:01,021 --> 00:18:02,765
the guy Niran always talked about

333
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:05,501
when he was trying out for the national team.

334
00:18:06,079 --> 00:18:07,583
Huh? Where did you see him?

335
00:18:07,968 --> 00:18:08,693
Here?

336
00:18:09,691 --> 00:18:10,323
Yeah.

337
00:18:10,936 --> 00:18:12,238
I saw him walking with Coach Ong.

338
00:18:12,781 --> 00:18:14,299
The student council was there too.

339
00:18:15,139 --> 00:18:18,602
I guess they were filming
promotional content for the tri-school game.

340
00:18:18,602 --> 00:18:19,799
It’s today.

341
00:18:20,009 --> 00:18:21,560
The basketball game looks so good.

342
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:23,896
The top contenders from the other schools
are fire.

343
00:18:24,246 --> 00:18:26,463
Who do we even have left from our school?

344
00:18:26,848 --> 00:18:28,512
Not many seniors are competing.

345
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:31,634
Why don’t you ask Cheewa?

346
00:18:31,757 --> 00:18:32,574
He’s preparing for the event.

347
00:18:32,574 --> 00:18:33,292
He should know.

348
00:18:34,448 --> 00:18:38,085
By the way, he’s been so busy
he hasn’t eaten with us for several days now.

349
00:18:38,260 --> 00:18:39,423
Have you talked to him at all?

350
00:18:39,966 --> 00:18:40,976
Not really.

351
00:18:41,414 --> 00:18:42,677
We’ve only seen each other in the car.

352
00:18:43,395 --> 00:18:44,585
He seems tired.

353
00:18:45,058 --> 00:18:46,570
He sleeps the whole way.

354
00:18:48,426 --> 00:18:51,886
When I saw Jomyut and Newton, they were
complaining that they were tired too.

355
00:18:53,287 --> 00:18:55,249
They have no time
to get on our nerves like before.

356
00:18:56,842 --> 00:18:57,986
I miss them.

357
00:18:58,074 --> 00:18:58,889
Those three with glasses.

358
00:19:00,255 --> 00:19:01,304
Glasses is here.

359
00:19:04,035 --> 00:19:04,761
Hey.

360
00:19:04,761 --> 00:19:05,606
What are you doing here?

361
00:19:05,851 --> 00:19:06,853
Don’t you have to work?

362
00:19:07,308 --> 00:19:08,384
I’m done with my work.

363
00:19:08,682 --> 00:19:10,869
The game starts at 1.
Wanna go watch?

364
00:19:11,009 --> 00:19:14,012
You mean basketball?

365
00:19:15,290 --> 00:19:17,127
Yes, come watch me compete.

366
00:19:18,143 --> 00:19:18,643
Huh?

367
00:19:19,483 --> 00:19:20,696
You’re competing in basketball?

368
00:19:22,114 --> 00:19:24,047
Yes, they were short on players,

369
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:25,728
so they asked me to fill in.

370
00:19:27,496 --> 00:19:29,027
Okay. Sure.

371
00:19:29,447 --> 00:19:30,563
We’ll go watch you.

372
00:19:30,983 --> 00:19:32,170
We’re free this afternoon.

373
00:19:34,411 --> 00:19:35,510
See you later.

374
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:43,816
Someone this timid
is competing in basketball?

375
00:19:44,324 --> 00:19:45,310
Does he even know how to play?

376
00:19:45,503 --> 00:19:46,718
Maybe he’s a substitute.

377
00:19:47,138 --> 00:19:48,283
He said they were short on players.

378
00:19:49,351 --> 00:19:51,423
But even though he’s a sub,
we need to go cheer him on.

379
00:19:51,598 --> 00:19:52,937
Yeah, I know.

380
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:54,892
So?

381
00:19:55,645 --> 00:19:57,061
Do we want to go wait at the court now?

382
00:19:58,707 --> 00:20:00,820
You’re so impatient.

383
00:20:04,164 --> 00:20:05,173
I don’t have anything else to do.

384
00:20:06,311 --> 00:20:07,786
Oh, I have class, but I’m not studying.

385
00:20:08,346 --> 00:20:09,043
Ugh.

386
00:20:09,043 --> 00:20:09,772
You’ll fall asleep.

387
00:20:10,035 --> 00:20:11,142
You should study for a change.

388
00:20:25,396 --> 00:20:26,301
There they are.

389
00:20:31,694 --> 00:20:33,360
You guys are late.

390
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,632
They’re about to start.

391
00:20:35,455 --> 00:20:36,139
Well,

392
00:20:36,297 --> 00:20:37,790
we were waiting for Hem
to get his meatballs.

393
00:20:38,455 --> 00:20:39,681
Where’s Cheewa?

394
00:20:39,681 --> 00:20:40,831
Has he gotten ready?

395
00:20:41,356 --> 00:20:43,644
Gotten ready? He’s already on the court.

396
00:20:53,038 --> 00:20:53,995
Damn.

397
00:20:54,258 --> 00:20:56,700
Niran, he’s a starter?

398
00:20:56,875 --> 00:20:57,800
So cool.

399
00:20:58,921 --> 00:21:00,027
Without his glasses too.

400
00:21:02,881 --> 00:21:05,561
Of course, Cheewa’s a starter.
He’s been practicing for a week.

401
00:21:05,789 --> 00:21:06,498
Oh.

402
00:21:07,373 --> 00:21:09,619
He said he was preparing for the event.

403
00:21:10,022 --> 00:21:12,480
I thought he was organizing it.

404
00:21:13,023 --> 00:21:15,031
He was organizing the event
and practicing basketball.

405
00:21:15,031 --> 00:21:16,167
That’s why he’s super exhausted.

406
00:21:16,990 --> 00:21:20,358
At first, we asked him
why he had to play basketball.

407
00:21:20,358 --> 00:21:22,177
Did you know what his answer was?

408
00:21:23,035 --> 00:21:26,058
He said he wanted to look cool
in front of the person he likes.

409
00:21:44,744 --> 00:21:45,804
Bravo!

410
00:22:03,315 --> 00:22:04,548
Are you waiting to talk to him?

411
00:22:05,126 --> 00:22:06,739
The judo match is about to start.

412
00:22:06,897 --> 00:22:07,684
Wanna watch it?

413
00:22:10,293 --> 00:22:11,072
You guys go ahead.

414
00:22:11,072 --> 00:22:11,923
I’ll catch up with you soon.

415
00:22:14,759 --> 00:22:15,522
- Alright.
- Okay.

416
00:22:15,732 --> 00:22:16,496
See you later.

417
00:22:19,281 --> 00:22:20,241
P’Cheewa, you’re so handsome.

418
00:22:20,626 --> 00:22:22,026
I’m your fan, P’Cheewa.

419
00:22:22,026 --> 00:22:23,513
We’re your biggest fans.

420
00:22:23,513 --> 00:22:24,280
You’re amazing.

421
00:22:25,505 --> 00:22:26,202
Thank you.

422
00:22:31,297 --> 00:22:32,154
Meow kiss, please.

423
00:22:36,321 --> 00:22:38,389
This camera too, please.

424
00:22:41,366 --> 00:22:42,401
You’re getting way too cool.

425
00:22:46,037 --> 00:22:47,930
Damn, Jace beat our school again.

426
00:22:55,230 --> 00:22:56,108
What’s wrong?

427
00:23:03,434 --> 00:23:04,135
Niran!

428
00:23:10,719 --> 00:23:12,340
I’m going to the Music Club with these two.

429
00:23:20,188 --> 00:23:20,959
Is something going on?

430
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:26,101
I just wanted to ask about our last match,
when you lost to me.

431
00:23:26,574 --> 00:23:27,990
You weren’t giving it your all, were you?

432
00:23:30,074 --> 00:23:31,941
You don’t usually slip up that easily.

433
00:23:32,816 --> 00:23:34,576
If you lost on purpose,

434
00:23:35,031 --> 00:23:36,453
just tell me honestly.

435
00:23:37,276 --> 00:23:38,806
I don’t want to win that way.

436
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:41,315
You…

437
00:23:42,190 --> 00:23:42,875
I’m what?

438
00:23:43,768 --> 00:23:44,826
Are you crazy?

439
00:23:45,509 --> 00:23:46,167
Huh?

440
00:23:47,235 --> 00:23:48,487
What kind of person do you think I am?

441
00:23:49,117 --> 00:23:50,527
Do you really think I’d want to lose to you?

442
00:23:50,790 --> 00:23:52,954
After that match, I was down for like a month.

443
00:23:53,409 --> 00:23:55,218
Why would I lose on purpose?

444
00:23:55,393 --> 00:23:56,308
What are you even thinking?

445
00:23:56,448 --> 00:23:57,886
Well, you’re usually better than me.

446
00:23:57,886 --> 00:23:59,967
Hey, rankings go up and down.

447
00:24:00,090 --> 00:24:01,654
No one stays at the top forever.

448
00:24:02,022 --> 00:24:03,616
I always give it my all.

449
00:24:04,054 --> 00:24:04,951
I never go easy on my opponents.

450
00:24:06,212 --> 00:24:08,031
I really lost. I admit it.

451
00:24:09,134 --> 00:24:10,039
And you…

452
00:24:10,599 --> 00:24:11,989
You won, so be proud of yourself.

453
00:24:13,512 --> 00:24:14,994
Give yourself some credit.

454
00:24:16,255 --> 00:24:18,140
Don’t think you won
because I went easy on you.

455
00:24:22,202 --> 00:24:23,504
I like someone cool like you.

456
00:24:23,627 --> 00:24:25,171
Of course. I’m Niran.

457
00:24:25,171 --> 00:24:26,519
Win or lose, I’m still cool.

458
00:24:26,729 --> 00:24:28,710
Can I get your number, cool guy?

459
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:30,347
What for?

460
00:24:40,876 --> 00:24:41,879
Why are you staring?

461
00:24:42,754 --> 00:24:43,782
What’s wrong, Cheewa?

462
00:24:44,587 --> 00:24:45,308
Nothing.

463
00:24:45,623 --> 00:24:46,350
That’s a lie.

464
00:24:47,558 --> 00:24:48,237
Yes.

465
00:24:49,025 --> 00:24:49,653
That’s a lie.

466
00:24:51,491 --> 00:24:53,308
Is Jace hitting on you?

467
00:24:54,341 --> 00:24:54,985
Huh?

468
00:24:56,298 --> 00:24:57,681
He asked for your number.

469
00:24:58,014 --> 00:24:59,237
Did you give it to him?

470
00:24:59,412 --> 00:25:00,775
What did you talk to him about?

471
00:25:00,775 --> 00:25:01,744
Did you two hit it off?

472
00:25:05,193 --> 00:25:07,708
Why? Are you jealous, kid?

473
00:25:10,282 --> 00:25:11,109
Am I allowed to be jealous?

474
00:25:12,650 --> 00:25:14,292
If so, I’m very jealous.

475
00:25:19,895 --> 00:25:21,235
Jace asked for my number.

476
00:25:21,848 --> 00:25:23,528
He said he wanted to get to know me better.

477
00:25:24,263 --> 00:25:25,050
But I didn’t give it to him.

478
00:25:25,925 --> 00:25:28,109
I said
we’re better off as rivals

479
00:25:28,389 --> 00:25:29,599
and that he shouldn’t
want to be something else.

480
00:25:31,595 --> 00:25:34,437
Whoa, that’s so harsh.

481
00:25:35,908 --> 00:25:38,795
I really believe that,
so I rejected him directly.

482
00:25:39,478 --> 00:25:43,593
So the fact that you didn’t reject me directly

483
00:25:44,136 --> 00:25:44,909
means…

484
00:25:46,467 --> 00:25:47,938
I have a chance to be something else?

485
00:25:52,788 --> 00:25:53,610
What about you, Cheewa?

486
00:25:56,450 --> 00:25:58,418
Don’t you have so many admirers yourself?

487
00:25:58,762 --> 00:26:00,167
You just took off your glasses
and played basketball.

488
00:26:00,429 --> 00:26:01,552
What’s with all that?

489
00:26:04,791 --> 00:26:06,389
They asked for photos with me.

490
00:26:06,862 --> 00:26:08,822
They just said I’m good at basketball.

491
00:26:10,906 --> 00:26:12,382
I didn’t know
you were that good at basketball.

492
00:26:13,850 --> 00:26:15,554
I beat you before, P’Niran.

493
00:26:17,025 --> 00:26:17,791
Am I cool?

494
00:26:25,056 --> 00:26:27,805
But now you’re cool
in other people’s eyes too.

495
00:26:30,081 --> 00:26:31,365
Let’s not talk about other people.

496
00:26:32,030 --> 00:26:35,813
In your eyes, am I any cool at all?

497
00:26:40,383 --> 00:26:41,489
Well…

498
00:26:47,943 --> 00:26:48,764
You’re pretty cool.

499
00:26:49,289 --> 00:26:50,020
Kinda cool.

500
00:26:53,067 --> 00:26:54,221
That’s enough.

501
00:26:55,989 --> 00:26:57,004
I told other people

502
00:26:58,037 --> 00:27:00,283
I’m already seeing someone.

503
00:27:01,193 --> 00:27:02,290
Since when
have you been seeing someone?

504
00:27:09,426 --> 00:27:10,259
Will you?

505
00:27:10,259 --> 00:27:10,997
Huh?

506
00:27:14,569 --> 00:27:16,620
Will P’Niran be Cheewa’s boyfriend?

507
00:27:24,952 --> 00:27:26,311
By the way, you said

508
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:28,463
you wanted to come over
and listen to the music my dad plays.

509
00:27:28,463 --> 00:27:28,963
But…

510
00:27:29,996 --> 00:27:32,329
you want me to listen to music at your house
as what, exactly?

511
00:27:32,329 --> 00:27:33,302
Hello.

512
00:27:33,302 --> 00:27:34,959
Come over as often as you like.

513
00:27:56,327 --> 00:27:58,611
Will your dad really be okay with this?

514
00:28:00,500 --> 00:28:01,164
Of course.

515
00:28:02,146 --> 00:28:03,617
I just don’t really invite anyone over.

516
00:28:04,138 --> 00:28:05,255
Thara was here once.

517
00:28:05,716 --> 00:28:08,157
He was hanging out for just a little while
before I kicked him out.

518
00:28:11,891 --> 00:28:13,426
Look at you, all stressed and down.

519
00:28:14,929 --> 00:28:15,901
Don’t be so down.

520
00:28:15,901 --> 00:28:17,610
You have me. I’ve got you.

521
00:28:18,875 --> 00:28:19,790
It’s my house.

522
00:28:20,846 --> 00:28:21,502
Okay?

523
00:28:21,904 --> 00:28:22,620
Okay.

524
00:28:23,156 --> 00:28:23,656
Come on.

525
00:28:38,988 --> 00:28:40,820
P’Niran, you’re talented just like your dad.

526
00:28:41,817 --> 00:28:42,772
Oh, my dad.

527
00:28:43,070 --> 00:28:44,899
If he hadn’t gotten so badly injured
that he couldn’t do judo anymore,

528
00:28:44,959 --> 00:28:46,793
he’d be so damn intense.

529
00:28:46,942 --> 00:28:48,200
Bam! Bam! Bam!

530
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:49,588
What are you teasing me about?

531
00:28:49,692 --> 00:28:50,632
Hello.

532
00:28:50,811 --> 00:28:51,459
Hello.

533
00:28:52,709 --> 00:28:56,421
Do you play any sports, Cheewa?

534
00:28:56,986 --> 00:28:59,906
I play some,
but I’m not very serious about it.

535
00:29:00,590 --> 00:29:03,053
He says he’s not very serious,
but he won a basketball game today.

536
00:29:04,542 --> 00:29:05,160
Wow.

537
00:29:05,428 --> 00:29:06,054
Amazing.

538
00:29:06,337 --> 00:29:06,905
Hey.

539
00:29:07,485 --> 00:29:11,905
Don’t you want to be a professional athlete?

540
00:29:12,947 --> 00:29:13,971
Hmm…

541
00:29:14,150 --> 00:29:17,142
Yeah, but it’s more like a hobby for me.

542
00:29:18,466 --> 00:29:20,082
Cheewa is good at everything.

543
00:29:20,082 --> 00:29:21,023
He can play guitar.

544
00:29:21,023 --> 00:29:21,691
He’s good at school.

545
00:29:21,691 --> 00:29:23,049
He’s good at everything he does.

546
00:29:23,183 --> 00:29:24,685
Niran, take it down a notch.

547
00:29:25,175 --> 00:29:26,816
I’m asking Cheewa,

548
00:29:27,158 --> 00:29:28,612
but you answer for him.

549
00:29:28,895 --> 00:29:31,202
You know everything about him, huh?

550
00:29:32,626 --> 00:29:33,320
What’s with you?

551
00:29:33,766 --> 00:29:36,050
Is P’Niran always this talkative?

552
00:29:36,050 --> 00:29:38,608
Oh, he was so chatty as a kid.

553
00:29:38,608 --> 00:29:39,881
He’d talk non-stop.

554
00:29:39,881 --> 00:29:40,381
Yeah.

555
00:29:40,664 --> 00:29:44,249
But now that he’s grown up,

556
00:29:44,383 --> 00:29:45,468
he won’t talk to me.

557
00:29:45,468 --> 00:29:46,820
He acts all cool.

558
00:29:48,353 --> 00:29:49,277
I talk to you.

559
00:29:50,556 --> 00:29:51,530
You’re the only one acting all cool.

560
00:29:52,245 --> 00:29:52,745
Hey.

561
00:29:52,745 --> 00:29:53,361
“Wanna eat?”

562
00:29:53,778 --> 00:29:54,731
“Do you want dinner?”

563
00:29:55,103 --> 00:29:55,663
Like this.

564
00:29:55,663 --> 00:29:56,523
Are you making fun of me?

565
00:29:57,267 --> 00:29:59,247
Don’t make me tell your stories.

566
00:29:59,678 --> 00:30:01,621
One day, he came home.

567
00:30:02,023 --> 00:30:03,322
I don’t know what had gotten into him.

568
00:30:03,322 --> 00:30:04,376
He went into the bathroom,

569
00:30:04,644 --> 00:30:07,278
turned on the shower, and cried under it.

570
00:30:07,992 --> 00:30:09,450
He was fully clothed, mind you.

571
00:30:09,450 --> 00:30:10,509
Whoa.

572
00:30:11,431 --> 00:30:12,262
When was that?

573
00:30:13,318 --> 00:30:15,316
Good thing he wasn’t singing too.

574
00:30:15,316 --> 00:30:18,016
Otherwise, it’d be too much.

575
00:30:18,343 --> 00:30:20,323
But P’Niran is a really good singer.

576
00:30:20,799 --> 00:30:21,653
Oh, you’re the best.

577
00:30:21,846 --> 00:30:22,809
Really?

578
00:30:23,270 --> 00:30:24,995
No need to get into this one.

579
00:30:24,995 --> 00:30:26,176
There are so many stories, especially

580
00:30:26,176 --> 00:30:27,880
from when he went to competitions.

581
00:30:28,073 --> 00:30:28,834
That’s enough, Dad.

582
00:30:28,834 --> 00:30:30,155
He didn’t want to go.

583
00:30:30,423 --> 00:30:32,846
Are you sure
you don’t want to stay for dinner?

584
00:30:33,054 --> 00:30:33,862
I won’t take long to cook.

585
00:30:34,100 --> 00:30:36,714
My friends are coming over
to celebrate at my house.

586
00:30:37,027 --> 00:30:39,169
Next time, I’ll take you up on that.

587
00:30:39,348 --> 00:30:40,028
Okay.

588
00:30:40,028 --> 00:30:40,758
No problem.

589
00:30:40,877 --> 00:30:42,545
Come over as often as you like.

590
00:30:42,843 --> 00:30:46,020
Make yourself at home here.

591
00:30:46,451 --> 00:30:48,281
I’m going to go prepare dinner.

592
00:30:48,281 --> 00:30:49,689
Okay. Bye.

593
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:53,184
Let’s go.

594
00:30:57,365 --> 00:30:58,505
My dad seems to like you.

595
00:30:58,639 --> 00:31:00,412
He doesn’t usually invite anyone
to stay for a meal.

596
00:31:01,543 --> 00:31:03,248
It was fun talking to him.

597
00:31:03,590 --> 00:31:05,022
I thought he’d be scary.

598
00:31:05,974 --> 00:31:08,730
Oh, no. He just acts scary,
but he’s nothing like that.

599
00:31:10,352 --> 00:31:11,686
He acts all cool just like you do.

600
00:31:11,686 --> 00:31:12,186
Huh?

601
00:31:13,763 --> 00:31:15,702
Can I really come to your house often?

602
00:31:16,148 --> 00:31:16,775
Of course.

603
00:31:16,775 --> 00:31:17,747
My dad already invited you.

604
00:31:18,982 --> 00:31:21,408
Do you want me to come?

605
00:31:21,958 --> 00:31:23,446
Well, yes.

606
00:31:23,446 --> 00:31:24,089
You can come.

607
00:31:24,848 --> 00:31:26,684
By the way, you said

608
00:31:27,115 --> 00:31:28,990
you wanted to come over
and listen to the music my dad plays.

609
00:31:29,526 --> 00:31:30,609
Remember that?

610
00:31:30,817 --> 00:31:31,582
I do.

611
00:31:31,790 --> 00:31:34,732
I said that while we were on the bus
to the science exhibition, but…

612
00:31:37,455 --> 00:31:39,876
you want me to listen to music at your house
as what, exactly?

613
00:31:43,506 --> 00:31:44,006
Huh?

614
00:31:47,620 --> 00:31:49,149
You haven’t given me an answer.

615
00:31:49,819 --> 00:31:50,503
What answer?

616
00:31:54,654 --> 00:31:56,061
I asked you to be my boyfriend.

617
00:32:08,074 --> 00:32:08,817
Well…

618
00:32:11,064 --> 00:32:12,546
Here we come, Mr. Parncheewa.

619
00:32:22,735 --> 00:32:25,434
Jomyut said
you’re going to order pizza, Cheewa.

620
00:32:29,034 --> 00:32:29,723
Let’s go.

621
00:32:33,368 --> 00:32:34,499
Where’s Newton?

622
00:32:34,663 --> 00:32:35,813
He’s running an errand with his family.

623
00:32:36,051 --> 00:32:36,690
Whoa.

624
00:32:36,854 --> 00:32:38,557
Who is more important, his family or us?

625
00:32:42,544 --> 00:32:44,461
Congrats, bro,
on winning the basketball game.

626
00:32:46,499 --> 00:32:46,999
Hey.

627
00:32:47,564 --> 00:32:48,769
I thought you were going to lose.

628
00:32:49,052 --> 00:32:51,072
The other team was so good.

629
00:32:51,072 --> 00:32:54,374
Cheewa might not look it,
but he’s actually good at so many things.

630
00:32:54,716 --> 00:32:56,490
He’s done everything in the universe.

631
00:32:56,787 --> 00:32:59,489
Cheewa, how many hours
do you have in a day?

632
00:32:59,593 --> 00:33:02,354
My parents always encourage me
to try different things.

633
00:33:02,681 --> 00:33:04,461
I can always figure out if I like them later.

634
00:33:05,681 --> 00:33:08,067
Have you tried judo?

635
00:33:09,867 --> 00:33:13,958
I took lessons for a little while
when I was a kid.

636
00:33:14,717 --> 00:33:16,255
I only got the basics.

637
00:33:18,606 --> 00:33:19,466
Where did you take your lessons?

638
00:33:30,659 --> 00:33:32,284
This is Parncheewa, everyone.

639
00:33:33,102 --> 00:33:35,227
He’s new. He’ll be practicing with us today.

640
00:33:36,819 --> 00:33:37,351
Why?

641
00:33:37,663 --> 00:33:39,128
Are you worried he’s better than you?

642
00:33:39,515 --> 00:33:40,513
Come on.

643
00:33:41,153 --> 00:33:42,194
You’re already good, man.

644
00:33:42,596 --> 00:33:43,186
Thank you.

645
00:33:43,186 --> 00:33:44,580
You’re the best in my heart.

646
00:33:45,681 --> 00:33:47,250
Thara, can you pass me that?

647
00:33:49,095 --> 00:33:50,421
No, the other one.

648
00:33:50,421 --> 00:33:53,104
So you really took judo lessons?

649
00:33:54,666 --> 00:33:55,534
Yes, I did.

650
00:33:56,635 --> 00:33:57,386
Why?

651
00:33:57,460 --> 00:33:58,873
Did you think I lied?

652
00:34:01,938 --> 00:34:02,780
No.

653
00:34:02,854 --> 00:34:04,087
It was just unexpected.

654
00:34:17,608 --> 00:34:18,108
Cheewa.

655
00:34:19,075 --> 00:34:19,702
Yes?

656
00:34:23,421 --> 00:34:24,980
Have we met before?

657
00:34:34,821 --> 00:34:36,625
I don’t know how you feel about me,

658
00:34:37,414 --> 00:34:39,248
but I really admire you.

659
00:34:39,650 --> 00:34:42,472
I’m impressed by everything you do.

660
00:35:05,075 --> 00:35:06,489
We’ve met before, haven’t we?

661
00:35:10,740 --> 00:35:12,807
My name’s Niran. I’m 8 years old.

662
00:35:13,732 --> 00:35:18,047
My name’s Cheewa. I’m 7 years old.

663
00:35:18,221 --> 00:35:20,651
Then P’Niran is older.

664
00:35:20,651 --> 00:35:22,230
Yes, P’Niran.

665
00:35:22,546 --> 00:35:25,566
From now on,
P’Niran will take care of you, Cheewa.

666
00:35:25,645 --> 00:35:26,145
Okay.

667
00:35:28,642 --> 00:35:29,645
Glasses, come here.

668
00:35:33,519 --> 00:35:34,981
Count one, two, three.

669
00:35:34,981 --> 00:35:36,439
P’Niran, you’re so good.

670
00:35:36,644 --> 00:35:39,216
You’re so small. How are you so good?

671
00:35:39,342 --> 00:35:41,603
It doesn’t matter if you’re big or small.

672
00:35:41,745 --> 00:35:43,554
It’s all about this.

673
00:35:44,328 --> 00:35:45,498
Your ribs?

674
00:35:46,683 --> 00:35:47,291
Ugh.

675
00:35:48,666 --> 00:35:49,514
Or…

676
00:35:50,130 --> 00:35:51,575
is it about

677
00:35:52,397 --> 00:35:53,313
your insides?

678
00:35:56,078 --> 00:35:57,575
It’s all about your heart.

679
00:35:57,575 --> 00:35:58,842
If you have the heart to fight,

680
00:35:59,032 --> 00:36:00,540
you can do anything.

681
00:36:01,614 --> 00:36:02,731
Come on, let’s try again.

682
00:36:02,857 --> 00:36:05,025
Really focus on P’Niran’s feet.

683
00:36:06,653 --> 00:36:09,363
Do you want me to focus on your feet
or your heart?

684
00:36:10,121 --> 00:36:13,378
Ugh!

685
00:36:13,862 --> 00:36:14,975
Cheewa!

686
00:36:18,626 --> 00:36:21,173
If you want snacks,
come hide here and eat them.

687
00:36:21,473 --> 00:36:23,703
If Coach sees you sneaking in snacks,

688
00:36:24,509 --> 00:36:25,877
you’ll have to mop the floor.

689
00:36:26,052 --> 00:36:27,765
You love snacking, P’Niran?

690
00:36:28,839 --> 00:36:29,489
Mm.

691
00:36:36,831 --> 00:36:39,328
You’re actually pretty heavy, Nong Cheewa.

692
00:36:42,472 --> 00:36:44,699
You can let me get down, P’Niran.

693
00:36:45,378 --> 00:36:46,460
I’ll be fine.

694
00:36:47,124 --> 00:36:48,696
Your legs still hurt.

695
00:36:49,660 --> 00:36:51,090
P’Niran can do this.

696
00:36:52,291 --> 00:36:53,928
You’re so amazing, P’Niran.

697
00:36:53,928 --> 00:36:57,444
One day, I’ll let you ride on my back too.

698
00:36:58,487 --> 00:36:59,366
I’ll be waiting.

699
00:37:00,630 --> 00:37:02,350
P’Niran, did you know

700
00:37:02,729 --> 00:37:07,560
Cheewa is a human
who’s good at keeping promises?

701
00:37:07,860 --> 00:37:09,593
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

702
00:37:12,311 --> 00:37:13,565
Dad, hurry!

703
00:37:13,565 --> 00:37:16,614
P’Niran is going to teach me
some new moves today.

704
00:37:18,131 --> 00:37:22,082
Parncheewa, today is your last judo lesson.

705
00:37:22,588 --> 00:37:24,870
We’re moving tomorrow.

706
00:37:27,209 --> 00:37:28,028
It’s okay.

707
00:37:28,186 --> 00:37:29,490
If you like taking judo lessons,

708
00:37:29,822 --> 00:37:31,243
I’ll find a new place for you.

709
00:37:31,433 --> 00:37:33,060
You’ll get to meet new friends too.

710
00:37:33,060 --> 00:37:35,663
But I don’t want to meet new friends.

711
00:37:40,688 --> 00:37:42,115
Let’s hurry.

712
00:37:42,492 --> 00:37:44,050
I don’t want to keep P’Niran waiting.

713
00:37:45,014 --> 00:37:45,746
Slow down.

714
00:37:45,983 --> 00:37:46,958
You don’t want to fall down the stairs.

715
00:37:46,958 --> 00:37:47,626
Slow down.

716
00:37:53,378 --> 00:37:55,429
Parncheewa,
are you waiting for Niran?

717
00:37:56,393 --> 00:37:59,557
His dad called this morning to say that
Niran wasn’t coming to practice today.

718
00:37:59,747 --> 00:38:02,190
Please practice with the others instead.

719
00:38:05,113 --> 00:38:06,261
That day,

720
00:38:07,825 --> 00:38:10,281
I felt like
I was being thrown to the floor

721
00:38:11,956 --> 00:38:13,215
because I knew

722
00:38:13,657 --> 00:38:15,667
it was the last day I’d get to see you.

723
00:38:17,168 --> 00:38:20,624
But I didn’t get to see you,

724
00:38:24,053 --> 00:38:25,916
or even get to say goodbye.

725
00:38:28,729 --> 00:38:32,550
JUDO COMPETITION
Then one day, I saw you again

726
00:38:34,888 --> 00:38:37,393
when you won a judo competition.

727
00:38:40,938 --> 00:38:42,459
PIANGNIRAN KITTIMETEE
MEKHINWIBOON SCHOOL (M.W.B.)
I was so happy.

728
00:38:46,425 --> 00:38:48,572
I was so happy I didn’t know what to do.

729
00:38:51,290 --> 00:38:54,598
So I asked Dad to let me take the entrance
exam for your high school right away.

730
00:38:55,815 --> 00:38:58,684
But later, I didn’t know how to act,

731
00:38:59,292 --> 00:39:02,077
so I pretended not to know you.

732
00:39:02,892 --> 00:39:07,125
Getting to know you again this time
makes me really happy.

733
00:39:08,342 --> 00:39:10,204
Whether you remember me or not,

734
00:39:10,789 --> 00:39:12,804
I’ve always remembered you.

735
00:39:13,973 --> 00:39:15,968
I don’t know how you feel about me,

736
00:39:17,596 --> 00:39:19,316
but I really admire you.

737
00:39:21,165 --> 00:39:22,943
I’ve liked you since back then.

738
00:39:26,198 --> 00:39:28,979
I’m impressed by everything you do.

739
00:39:33,704 --> 00:39:35,727
No matter how you end up feeling about me,

740
00:39:38,713 --> 00:39:42,731
I’ll still like you anyway.

741
00:39:43,205 --> 00:39:44,789
No matter then or now.

742
00:39:47,064 --> 00:39:48,024
Thank you.

743
00:39:51,690 --> 00:39:53,405
Just having you in front of me right now

744
00:39:56,694 --> 00:39:58,274
already makes me the happiest.

745
00:40:03,721 --> 00:40:04,336
Mm.

746
00:40:11,322 --> 00:40:12,067
Cheewa.

747
00:40:16,175 --> 00:40:17,783
What if I asked you back?

748
00:40:23,267 --> 00:40:24,066
Will you be my boyfriend?

749
00:40:27,922 --> 00:40:31,492
♪ Is this love I feel, am I calling it right? ♪

750
00:40:31,492 --> 00:40:35,151
♪ Is it why my heart beats faster tonight? ♪

751
00:40:35,309 --> 00:40:36,053
Will you?

752
00:40:40,067 --> 00:40:41,870
Will P’Niran be Cheewa’s boyfriend?

753
00:40:42,739 --> 00:40:45,810
♪ I see you every day ♪

754
00:40:45,810 --> 00:40:48,836
♪ Yet I miss you again ♪

755
00:40:48,836 --> 00:40:52,749
♪ Is this love I feel, can you lend me a hand? ♪

756
00:40:52,749 --> 00:40:56,725
♪ Come and help this heart understand ♪

757
00:40:56,725 --> 00:40:57,536
- Yes!
- Yes!

758
00:40:57,694 --> 00:41:01,005
♪ This feeling that I have ♪

759
00:41:01,005 --> 00:41:05,599
♪ Oh tell me, is this love? ♪

760
00:41:19,540 --> 00:41:21,668
This is how a love nerd is.

761
00:41:22,158 --> 00:41:23,738
I’m only like this with you, P’Niran.

762
00:41:23,738 --> 00:41:24,482
Hey, guys.

763
00:41:24,624 --> 00:41:26,211
This is Nong Cheewa.

764
00:41:26,369 --> 00:41:27,419
I asked him to play the drums.

765
00:41:27,419 --> 00:41:28,653
You want Cheewa to play the drums?

766
00:41:28,779 --> 00:41:29,781
Does he know how to play?

767
00:41:30,002 --> 00:41:31,639
Is there anything you can’t do?

768
00:41:32,081 --> 00:41:33,325
It seems like you can do everything.

769
00:41:34,036 --> 00:41:35,898
I want you to be happy, P’Niran.

770
00:41:36,012 --> 00:41:37,590
You’re spoiling me rotten, you know?

771
00:41:38,106 --> 00:41:39,635
But aren’t you happy?

772
00:41:40,141 --> 00:41:41,701
If you are, then let yourself be spoiled rotten.

773
00:41:41,812 --> 00:41:43,031
I like every version of you.
